name amiri
category Package
revision 55403
shortdesc A classical Arabic typeface, Naskh style
longdesc Amiri is a classical Arabic typeface in Naskh style for
longdesc typesetting books and other running text. It is a revival of
longdesc the beautiful typeface pioneered in the early 20th century by
longdesc Bulaq Press in Cairo, also known as Amiria Press, after which
longdesc the font is named. The project aims at the revival of the
longdesc aesthetics and traditions of Arabic typesetting, and adapting
longdesc it to the era of digital typesetting, in a publicly available
longdesc form.
